<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian 91-day T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 91-day treasury bills fell to 10.248 percent from 10.257 percent at the previous auction on October 10.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: Jan 16, 1997 (Jan 9, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 10.248 percent (10.257)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 659.150 million (649.175 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 721.150 million (734.175 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 10.002-10.293 percent (10.002-10.297)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 10.002-10.500 percent (10.002-11.500)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 158 (188)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 163 (192)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
